 ## Unreleased
 
+### PokeMan Journey v5.5 — three original encounter families
+
+- Added nine permanent custom creatures at consecutive compatibility slots
+  **#405–413**: Finrush → Riptalon → Tsunamight, Geckore → Craguan →
+  Monolisk, and Kindlet → Raptorch → Pyrenix. Each base form evolves at level
+  16 and each middle form evolves at level 36.
+- The lines use the requested type progressions: Water → Water →
+  Water/Fighting; Grass → Grass → Grass/Rock; and Fire → Fire → Fire/Flying.
+- Added the custom abilities **Lightspeed**, **Stoneheart**, and **Rekindle**,
+  plus the signature attacks **Tidal Blitz**, **Verdant Crush**, and
+  **Phoenix Rush**.
+- These creatures do **not** replace the existing starters. Finrush is a 15%
+  Route 25 surfing encounter at levels 22–24; Geckore is a 15% Rock Tunnel 1F
+  encounter at levels 15–17; and Kindlet is a 15% Mt. Ember exterior encounter
+  at levels 32–34. Only the base stages occur in the wild.
+- The base-stage sprites and Pokédex sizes are deliberately tiny, the middle
+  forms show a strong growth jump, and the final forms fill the 64×64 battle
+  frame with massive height and weight entries.
+- Added normal and shiny palettes, front/back battle graphics, icons,
+  footprints, follower graphics, level-up learnsets, teachable moves, cries,
+  Pokédex entries, and save-compatible permanent evolutions for all nine.
+
+### PokeMan Journey v5.4.1 — early Kanto return
+
+- Added the intended early regional round trip: immediately after receiving
+  the Johto starter, speaking with Professor Elm can return the player to
+  Cinnabar Island to finish Kanto without defeating either region's Elite
+  Four. The Johto party is stored safely using the existing region-transfer
+  rules, and an early HUB PASS return resumes at New Bark Town until Goldenrod
+  City has actually been visited.
+- This is a save-compatible follow-up to v5.4; no new save is required when
+  continuing a clean canonical-roster playthrough.
+
+### PokeMan Journey v5.4 — canonical roster reset
+
+- Removed every custom Pokémon from the **playable roster**: Phycub, Embruin,
+  Infernursa, Psyshell, Verdachell, Astrachell, Amphid, Amphlume, Amphidrake,
+  Joeyro, Kickaroo, Kangarooze, Fintom, Hauntide, Sharkraith, Danyip, Danny,
+  and Danimal can no longer be selected, gifted, encountered, or substituted
+  into a trainer party. The active game is back to official Pokémon.
+- Restored Kanto's opening choices to **Bulbasaur, Mudkip, and Cyndaquil**.
+  Gary again uses the matching official-species rival branches and walks to
+  the physical ball containing his selection.
+- Restored Mt. Moon 1F's Zubat/Geodude/Paras table, Route 1's Rattata slot,
+  and the Abandoned Ship's Tentacruel slot. The Seafoam Islands pickup and
+  Mt. Ember Explosion tutor also no longer award custom Pokémon.
+- Restored Erika's post-Rainbow-Badge official starter recovery gift, while
+  keeping the existing Blaine recovery gift and all original-386 acquisition
+  paths.
+- Kept the complete Kanto → Johto → Hoenn progression, adjusted level/EXP
+  curve, always-obey behavior, fossil recovery, Pokédex location fixes, all
+  24 badges, and the level-80 final-reward Mew.
+- Custom source art and design data remain archived and disconnected so they
+  can be reused later in a genuinely original rebuild without appearing in
+  this game. Compatibility data is retained only to prevent older v5.1-v5.3
+  saves that already contain a custom Pokémon from crashing.
+
+> For a completely canonical roster, start a **new v5.4 save**. An older save
+> may still physically contain a previously caught custom Pokémon; v5.4 will
+> load it safely, but provides no way to obtain another one.
+
+### PokeMan Journey v5.3 — Danyip family
+
+- Added **Danyip → Danny → Danimal**, a pure Normal-type Field Egg Group
+  family at National Dex numbers **#402–404**. Danyip evolves at level 16 and
+  Danny at level 32; the line has its full requested stats, growth, friendship,
+  level-up moves, teachables, Pokédex entries, footprints, cries, menu icons,
+  front/back battle art, follower art, and charcoal/chocolate shiny palette.
+- Danyip is a **10% Route 1 grass encounter at levels 3–5** in both the
+  FireRed and LeafGreen encounter tables. The other Route 1 staples remain.
+- Added the custom **Annoy** ability (AI rating 3): after an opponent directly
+  inflicts burn, poison/toxic poison, paralysis, sleep, freeze, or frostbite,
+  the holder barks and tries to confuse that exact source. Annoy does not react
+  to self/ally status, Rest, hazards, weather, held items, or failed attempts,
+  and it uses the engine's normal Own Tempo, Safeguard, Substitute, terrain,
+  and existing-confusion protections.
+- Added focused Annoy battle regressions covering all status classes, Rest,
+  Toxic Spikes, failed and allied attempts, double-battle source selection,
+  Own Tempo, Substitute, and repeat activation after curing. Existing
+  Synchronize tests remain part of the full battle suite.
+- The ROM now identifies itself as **v5.3**. The opening screen says
+  **PokeMan Journey by xecho3x** instead of presenting the upstream Pokémon
+  World creator as the creator of this edition; upstream attribution remains
+  intact in `CREDITS.md`.
+
+### PokeMan Journey v5.2 custom families
+
+- Kanto now opens with three original starter lines: **Psyshell → Verdachell →
+  Astrachell** (Psychic/Grass), **Amphid → Amphlume → Amphidrake**
